 **Parameters:**
-*   **Resolution Constraint Function:** The specific logic for $R_c$. Can be user-defined bounds or a complex function [S1, unofficial][S2]. Typical example values from human tissue data: pink channel at $l_3$, orange channel at $l_5/l_4/l_0$, and rest at $l_0$ [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Resolution Levels:** Discrete levels $l_0, \dots, l_{max}$. $l_0$ is the highest resolution level [S1, unofficial][S2].
+*   **Resolution Constraint Function:** $R_c$ determines the resolution level for channel $c$ at position $p$ and ray parameter $t$ [S1, unofficial][S2]. It can be user-defined upper and lower bounds or a function incorporating frequency content, viewing parameters, and transfer functions [S1, unofficial][S2]. Typical example values from human tissue data: pink channel at $l_3$, orange channel at $l_5/l_4/l_0$, and rest at $l_0$ [S1, unofficial].
+*   **Resolution Levels:** Discrete levels $l_0, \dots, l_{max}$ where $l_0$ is the highest resolution (finest grid) and higher $l$ values represent coarser resolutions [S1, unofficial][S2].
 
